# Security Policy

<!-- Per-repo. Fill in supported versions before committing. Rename to
     SECURITY.md (drop .example) so GitHub's own vulnerability-reporting
     UI picks it up. Requires GitHub private vulnerability reporting
     enabled on the repo (Settings, Security, Private vulnerability
     reporting). Delete this comment before committing a filled copy. -->

## Supported Versions

| Version | Supported |
|---------|-----------|
| 1.x     | Yes       |
| < 1.0   | No        |

## Scope

In scope: code and configuration in this repository. Out of scope:
third-party dependencies and actions (report to their own maintainers),
social engineering, and physical attacks.

## Reporting a Vulnerability

Report vulnerabilities through GitHub's private vulnerability reporting
(Security tab, Report a vulnerability). Do not open a public issue for a
vulnerability report.

Response time: acknowledgment within 5 business days. Remediation
target: 30 days from acknowledgment.

## Disclosure Policy

Coordinated disclosure. Report stays private until a fix ships or 90
days pass, whichever comes first.
